# All Features Runner

Use this rule when the user asks to run all features, the complete functional suite, every feature, or to diagnose the whole Spectrum Back Office test suite.

Run from the workspace root with a headless browser:

```powershell
$env:HEADED = 'false'
npm run test:headless
```

Capture the exit code and complete Cucumber summary. Do not report a pass when the process times out, is cancelled, produces no summary, or has no reliable exit code. Never expose `.env` values, credentials, tokens, cookies, or authorization headers. Do not generate reports or use stale report files as evidence.

For each failure, isolate the relevant feature with `features/functional/<feature>.feature --format progress`, then isolate by exact scenario name only when needed. Record the failed step, owning file/method, locator/assertion/action, phase, current evidence, and cause category: configuration, authentication, shared setup/navigation, selector, timing, data, assertion, teardown, or live environment.

When the user authorizes a fix, make the smallest evidence-based change in the owning hook, page object, step, utility, or setup code. Do not weaken assertions, skip scenarios, add arbitrary sleeps, or change unrelated features. Run `npm run typecheck` after every fix, then rerun `npm run test:headless`. Stop only when the complete suite passes or a live-environment blocker is proven. Report features/scenarios, passed/failed/skipped/undefined, exit code, evidence, fixes, and remaining blockers.
